From b0ea3433e8f28562dc02f7a6deff13c3cbb56492 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:57:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sim): share unchanged cut bricks between playback
 keyframes

A playback keyframe was a whole copy of the cut layers. The cut layers
now hold each brick in an Arc: a clone copies the keys and the pointers,
and a write copies a brick first when a clone still holds it. The
keyframe store counts a keyframe by the bricks that the keyframe before
it does not share, and by its map entries. claim_record and up_record
read the cell first, so a move that changes no cell copies no brick.

Dense 100 mm face (release): 68 keyframes hold 65.2 MB; whole copies
cost 444.9 MB (factor 6.8). The replay stays the live cut bit for bit.

Fixes #2194

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
